    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (77.33) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.93) anchoring the lineup, representing our highest-ceiling plays. **Trea Turner** faces a favorable matchup against the right-handed Dollander (4.41 xERA), with the added benefit of a slow-to-the-plate pitcher increasing his elite stolen base potential. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns a massive efficiency bump due to his matchup against Kumar Rocker; the combination of a positive platoon split and a pitcher who effectively gifts 100% stolen base opportunity makes him an auto-start despite the lower batting order position. **Kyle Schwarber** (70.60) rounds out our top-tier targets, leveraging his high xwOBA against Dollander to maximize run and RBI potential from the two-hole.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Hyeseong Kim** (36.38) on the bench. While his baseline talent remains solid, he drew a brutal assignment against Chris Sale (2.94 xERA), and the negative platoon disadvantage against the lefty essentially cratered his daily efficiency score, making him a clear sit compared to the upside offered by **Carson Benge** (57.05) or **Luke Raley** (56.73). We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Junior Caminero**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Carson Benge**, **Luke Raley**, and **Kazuma Okamoto**; any major shifts in order\u2014specifically if **Yordan Alvarez** moves out of the top two spots or **Junior Caminero** slips down the order\u2014may necessitate a re-evaluation of the bench depth provided by **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, or **Pedro Ramirez**. Owners should remain cautious of the volatility in the **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith** slots against Kris Bubic, as their lower scores reflect the narrow margin between a strong start and a benching to preserve precious games-played caps.",
